-- title:
--   Supersingularity of the universal j-invariant at 𝔭
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ and $\ell$ be primes with $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$, let $M'\neq 0$ with $q\nmid M'$ and $\ell\mid M'$, let $L$ be a characteristic-zero field which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb Q$ of order $q\ell$, and let $\zeta,\xi\in L$ be primitive $q$-th and $q\ell$-th roots of unity with $\zeta=\xi^{\ell}$. Let $H_1\le(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/\ell)^\times$, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ over $L$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field `xHFunctionField (q^2*M') H₁`. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, with uniformiser $\varpi$, and with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j\in K$, $j\neq 0$, have Laurent series the image of the classical $j$ $q$-expansion `jq`. On the two-chart integral model $X=$ `TwoChartIntegralModel A K j` (pushout of the spectra of the subalgebras of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, resp. over $A[j^{-1}]$), let $z\in X$ be a point at which the germ of $\varpi$, pulled back along $X\to\operatorname{Spec}A$, lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and let $y\in\operatorname{Spec}(\mathtt{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j)$ lie over $z$; assume that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring map from the chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the image of $j$ lies in `ssJSet q Ω`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion affine point. Finally let $D$ be a level moduli datum over a ring $A_0$ acting on $K$, let $P_0$ be a fine package for $D$ with representing ring $B_0$ and universal point, and let $x\in D.\mathrm{Pt}\,K$ have $j$-invariant equal, in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$, to `jqNModC L q`, the substitution $\mathsf q\mapsto\mathsf q^{q}$ in the $j$ $q$-expansion over $L$; assume the classifying map $P_0.\mathtt{classify}\,x:B_0\to K$ has image exactly the chart algebra. Writing $\theta$ for this map corestricted to the chart algebra and $\mathfrak p=\theta^{-1}(y)$, the conclusion is that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:B_0\to\Omega$ with $\ker\varphi=\mathfrak p$, the image $\varphi(P_0.j_0)$ of the package's universal $j$-invariant lies in `ssJSet q Ω`. The statement also names the stalk at $z$, its adic completion with respect to the maximal ideal, the completion map and the germ map from the chart algebra into the stalk; these abbreviations do not occur in the final assertion.
--
--   This is the transfer of supersingularity from the $j$-invariant of the $j$-finite chart of the two-chart integral model, at a point of the characteristic-$q$ fibre, to the universal $j$-invariant of the fine level-moduli package at the corresponding prime $\mathfrak p$; it is the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-style auxiliary-level variant, with no lower bound imposed on $q$. It feeds the two existence results in the `AuxLevelOne` namespace that produce ring isomorphisms between adic completions of stalks of the integral model and completions on the moduli side.
